			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement RBAC engine for IPC permission validation\n\nIntroduce a new `ValidatePermission` module within the Mountain backend to enforce role-based access control on IPC operations. This replaces implicit trust with a strict default-deny policy governed by `SecurityContext` envelopes and a configurable `Validator` engine.\n\nThe implementation includes:\n- `SecurityContext::Struct`: Per-request metadata capturing user identity, assigned roles, direct permissions, origin IP, and timestamps.\n- `Validator::Struct`: The core engine managing role/permission registries and operation-to-permission mappings (e.g., `file:write` requires `file.write`).\n- Core validation logic supporting timeout enforcement, role aggregation, and default-deny semantics.\n- Initialization routines for default roles (`user`, `developer`, `admin`) and standard permission sets.\n\nThis refactors the IPC security layer to align with the distributed architecture's requirement for explicit, auditable access control between the UI (Wind/Sky) and native backend (Mountain). All units follow the project's strict PascalCase naming convention and modular 'one export per file' pattern.",
			"SHA": "bfa9282db74c891c0aebc6d9afc3fbccdb1b2277"
		},
